                <pb facs="0509" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg421"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Strobel to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1888</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 356.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that I have on
                    this date recalled the attention of the minister of state to the subject of an
                    indemnity to Mr. Doane, the American missionary, in the sense indicated in the
                    Department’s No. 324, of the 20th ultimo.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward H. Strobel</hi>.<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
